## Course Overview

This graduate-level course introduces inverse problems as a unified framework for understanding modern medical imaging systems. The course covers mathematical foundations, forward and adjoint operators, optimization, and iterative reconstruction methods, with applications to X-ray CT, MRI, electrical impedance tomography, ptychography, and ultrasound tomography.

